<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4. Results and Inference Performance ‣ Serving LLMs in HPC Clusters: A Comparative Study of Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra and High-Performance GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> highlights QAic’s throughput advantage in single-card setups: for TinyLlama-1.1B, it achieves 7,346.6 tokens/s (1 card) versus H200’s 3,669.6 tokens/s (1 card).
Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4. Results and Inference Performance ‣ Serving LLMs in HPC Clusters: A Comparative Study of Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra and High-Performance GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> corroborates QAic’s power efficiency, with its 149.9 watt consumption for GPT-2-117M dwarfing A100’s 415.9 watt.
However, exceptions like Granite-20B (-4 tokens/(sec <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> watt)) and DeepSeek-70B (-1.1 tokens/(sec <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> watt)) in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4. Results and Inference Performance ‣ Serving LLMs in HPC Clusters: A Comparative Study of Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra and High-Performance GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> suggest architectural trade-offs at extreme scales.
Overall, QAic’s single-card performance and <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math>441.3 watt peak power (Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4. Results and Inference Performance ‣ Serving LLMs in HPC Clusters: A Comparative Study of Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra and High-Performance GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) position it as a compelling solution for energy-conscious deployments, particularly for models under 32B parameters.</p>
</div>
